{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. Further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct NodePhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.NodePhase`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `NodePhase` is the public marker type for an `Ask` request that has begun collecting node contents.\n2. A request enters that phase once a node input has been added.\n3. More node inputs can still be added while in that phase.\n4. The request can then be awaited for the answer.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` carries a `{test}` reference to `NodePhase`.\n- The test builds the request as `ctx.ask::<Answer>().context(...)`, which is the context phase.\n- `.contents_of_current_node()` then moves it into `Ask<..., NodePhase>`. In `procedure.rs`, `contents_of_current_node` returns `Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, NodePhase>` via `into_node_phase`.\n- From that phase the test chains `.contents_of_successors(7)` and `.contents_of_current_node()` again. These further inputs are accepted in the node phase, which covers \"further node inputs can be added\".\n- The test then calls `.into_future()` and awaits. `await_phase!(NodePhase)` provides `IntoFuture` for that phase, so this covers \"before awaiting the answer\".\n- The test asserts the outcome: the decoded answer is `n == 7`, and the agent receives the insertions in order, `[1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`, with repetition.\n- It also asserts that the reads and the recorded dependencies match.\n- It checks that the future is `Send` and that the schema is passed to the agent.\n\n**Other considerations**\n- `contents_of_successors` as the first node input is not tested separately. It uses the same transition code as `contents_of_current_node`, so it is not a distinct case.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` covers the public export of the type through its own requirement. It is not needed for the behavior assessed here.\n- Excluding `.context()` after the node phase is enforced at compile time by the type-state design. The requirement text does not state it as an obligation.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "909f09d5168c839a764d052216fd8a81d52222d7dce5a9a991746bb17ad69803",
